{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through both. “Nontrivial” is the model-checking term (a strongly connected component with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at least one edge, as in Büchi-automaton emptiness checks); this is NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strongly_connected_components"},{"type":"text","text":" filtered to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"len(c) > 1 or G.has_edge(v, v)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift#L89","fileName":"NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponentsSays10ArraySliceVy6VertexQzGGyF","title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","text":"ArraySlice"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Connectivity"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass, O(V + E): a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s successors, so a single-vertex component costs nothing more.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The components are those of "},{"code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" without the trivial ones, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order. Empty exactly when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in "},{"code":"attractingComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices do not start at 0."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":", so one sort by that vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position puts the components in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"text":", where positions are insertion order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedGraph"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivit